Z||000004||1FieroGTRacingInc||05-18-2000||01:34 PM||||ooooook....  I am sooo confused.  a code 12 blink's 3 time..??..  i went to the link's , and ???   <BR>      <BR>when i jump it and turn on the key..  it blink's 2 times....   then..... it blink's 3 times....  soooooo does that mean that i have a code 12 ????  OK if I have a code 12 ...  WHAT IS A CODE 12??    LOL   please help me...  give me some more link's for me to figure it out ...  thank everybody for the help..               Steve...||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FieroGTRacingInc||05-18-2000||01:38 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by bHooper:<BR><B>code 23 is the MAT sensor.  Take a look at the link below.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/v6help/code23.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.franken.de/users/dagobah/luke/v6help/code23.html</A> <P>hoop</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>bHooper.......   why did you give me that for a code 23....   it blink's 2 times...  then 3 times....  soooo  does that mean  a 23????  steve   thank you bHooper<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||triker||05-18-2000||01:48 PM||||When you turn on the key with the jumper in place, you should get 3 flashes of code 12, - --, - --, - -- then whatever trouble codes are stored.  Code 23 would repeat 3 times as -- ---.  After all codes have shown, it will start over again.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-18-2000||01:49 PM||||If you jumper the ALDL connector, Then turn the key on (not starting the engine) The SES light should blink once, pause then blink twice. This is code 12. It is a normal thing. It will do this 3 times. Then it will begin blinking the codes stored. Example would be 2 blinks, pause then 3 blinks is code 23. 4 blinks pause 4 blinks is code 44. All codes are repeated 3 times. If you do not see the code 12 problem may be in the ECM itself. Also make sure you are putting the jumper in the right pins.||||reg||1
Z||000008||mbramble||05-18-2000||01:52 PM||||From the first link I provided above"<P>"Turn the ignition key to the "run" position but don't start, and the Service Engine Soon light will blink the codes, starting with the code 12 (three times) and continuing with the real trouble codes (each three times), followed by the code 12 again to signify "that's all, folks!"  "<P>A code 12 (the starting code) is  " blink pause blink-blink " it goes three times.  Then each code blinks three times.  If it's a 23 you will get <BR>blink-blink pause blink-blink-blink (3 times) then the next code.  If it's a code 12, it is starting over again.  There is no code 2 or code 3.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||1FieroGTRacingInc||05-18-2000||02:06 PM||||Thank's EVERYONE...  I feel soo dumb ...  but i just didnt know i guess....  Steve||||reg||1
Z||000010||1FieroGTRacingInc||05-18-2000||02:45 PM||||Well....  I went out there and all it does is ....  blink..... blink,blink...  which is a code 12 , correct?  which from what i see it means all is normal??   sorry for all the ?'s, and problem's...    <BR>                                Steve||||reg||1
Z||000011||Old Lar||05-18-2000||04:20 PM||||It means there are no codes stored.  Something else may be wrong but not tripping an error code.||||reg||1
Z||000012||theogre||05-18-2000||06:42 PM||||What lar said. The ECM will flash the 12 sequence forever if no codes are there. if there is a real code your get 3 12's then what ever codes 3 times each. after the last code the 12's will start again.<P>so *.**..*.**..*.**..**.***..**.***..**.***..*.**..*.**..*.** (*= light flash .= pause time) would be 12 12 12 23 23 23 12 12 12 and that would be a MAT sensor failure code.<P>I've never had a problem reading the codes when I first dealt with them, they where plain as day. This thread made me think about this a bit then I realized why. The fire department in the town I lived in used to use horn codes the same way to tell firemen where the fire is instead of just simple siren. At one time I had the whole horn card memorized. <p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 05-18-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000013||1FieroGTRacingInc||05-18-2000||07:12 PM||||Sooo, I need the Fire Dept. ???  ||||reg||1
